## Summary of Architecture Patterns

### Tool Package Structure
```
packages/tools/official/{tool-name}/
├── package.json              # Must export dist/{index.d.ts,index.js}
├── tsconfig.json             # Extends @tpmjs/tsconfig/base.json
├── tsup.config.ts            # ESM build config with dts: true
├── block.ts                  # Optional: metadata for validators
├── index.ts                  # Optional: re-export from src/
└── src/
    └── index.ts              # Main implementation
        ├── Interfaces for results (typed outputs)
        ├── Input types (for schema)
        ├── Helper functions (validation, formatting, etc.)
        └── Export const toolName = tool({ description, inputSchema, async execute })
```

### Tool Implementation Pattern
```typescript
import { jsonSchema, tool } from 'ai';

// 1. Define result type
export interface ToolResult {
  /* structured output */
}

// 2. Define input type
type ToolInput = {
  param1: string;
  param2?: number;
  _sandboxWorkDir?: string;  // Only for sandbox tools
};

// 3. Export tool function
export const toolName = tool({
  description: 'Clear, production-focused description',
  inputSchema: jsonSchema<ToolInput>({
    type: 'object',
    properties: { /* ... */ },
    required: ['param1'],
    additionalProperties: false,
  }),
  async execute(input): Promise<ToolResult> {
    // Validate
    // Execute
    // Return structured result
  },
});

export default toolName;
```

### blocks.yml Tool Definition Pattern
```yaml
  namespace.toolName:
    type: utility                          # or service, computation
    description: "Human-readable..."
    path: "tool-folder-name"               # Where in packages/tools/official/
    domain_rules:                          # What validators check
      - id: rule_id
        description: "Implementation requirement"
    inputs:
      - name: param_name
        type: string|number|object|array
        description: "..."
        optional: true
    outputs:
      - name: result
        type: ResultType
        description: "..."
        measures: [working_implementation, valid_output_structure, proper_error_handling, ai_sdk_compliance]
```

### Sandbox Tool Pattern
- Each tool receives `_sandboxWorkDir` parameter (injected by server, not user-provided)
- All file paths are resolved relative to workspace
- Security: validate paths don't escape with `Deno.realPath()`
- Output: truncate stdout/stderr at 100KB, file reads at 500KB
- Timeouts: default 30s, max 5min, with SIGTERM -> SIGKILL escalation
- Results: Always include `truncated: boolean` flag

